    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d446">

                <pb facs="0514" n="502" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg502"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.2221/326: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-04-05T19:00:00-05:00">April 5, 1937—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>160. Your 446,<anchor n="57a" xml:id="d446-f1"/> arrest volunteers. Advise Consul
                    George obtain and forward Department names and passport data of each and names
                        <pb facs="0515" n="503" xml:id="pg503"/> and addresses of persons who will
                    pay for maintenance and return passage to United States. Consul should
                    understand and make clear to all the authorities concerned that these persons
                    were proceeding to Spain in violation of this Government’s stipulations. Cable
                    briefly report.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
